Make the advertised AirPlay device model configurable

shairport-sync hardcodes "Shairport Sync" as the model in the mDNS TXT
records (am=/model=) and the AirPlay 2 /info plist. Senders derive the
device icon in their AirPlay picker from this string, so a configurable
model lets the speaker choose its icon (e.g. "AudioAccessory5,1" shows
a HomePod mini). New option: general.airplay_device_model, default
unchanged.

Upstream has declined an option for this; carried locally by boompi.

--- a/common.h	2025-01-31 06:57:31
+++ b/common.h	2026-08-06 02:40:48
@@ -134,6 +134,8 @@
   char *password;
   char *service_name; // the name for the shairport service, e.g. "Shairport Sync Version %v running
                       // on host %h"
+  char *airplay_device_model; // advertised model ("am="/"model=" TXT records and the AirPlay 2
+                              // /info plist). Senders pick their device icon from this.
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_PA
   char *pa_server;           // the pulseaudio server address that Shairport Sync will play on.
--- a/shairport.c	2025-01-31 06:57:31
+++ b/shairport.c	2026-08-06 02:40:48
@@ -588,6 +588,13 @@
       if (config_lookup_string(config.cfg, "general.name", &str)) {
         raw_service_name = (char *)str;
       }
+
+      /* Get the advertised AirPlay device model, e.g. "AudioAccessory5,1".
+         Senders derive the device icon shown in their AirPlay picker from
+         this; default is "Shairport Sync" (generic speaker icon). */
+      if (config_lookup_string(config.cfg, "general.airplay_device_model", &str)) {
+        config.airplay_device_model = (char *)str;
+      }
 #ifdef CONFIG_LIBDAEMON
       /* Get the Daemonize setting. */
       config_set_lookup_bool(config.cfg, "sessioncontrol.daemonize_with_pid_file", &daemonisewith);
